#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:3
#: b622436f8c3844c6b8a5c1d2d8e31f61
msgid "Qrexec: socket-based services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:6
#: 595280310b6c4bfc99b268e9f12e3d13
msgid ""
"*This page describes how to implement and use new socket-backed services for "
"qrexec. See* :doc:`qrexec </developer/services/qrexec>` *for general "
"overview of the qrexec framework.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:8
#: b0fd32e426ea45fb88f8fde1c8e6c1fa
msgid ""
"As of Qubes 4.1, qrexec allows implementing services not only as executable "
"files, but also as Unix sockets. This allows Qubes RPC requests to be "
"handled by a server running in a VM and listening for connections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:11
#: 61511fc8b9604bd69cc91848d7e27f7b
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:14
#: 0b9f3166badf4d35875681141ed9ffe5
msgid ""
"When a Qubes RPC service is invoked, qrexec searches for a file that handles "
"it in the qubes-rpc directories (``/etc/qubes-rpc`` or ``/usr/local/etc/"
"qubes-rpc``). If the file is a Unix socket, qrexec will try to connect to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:16
#: 93e5a67aef924b45bc982ec8ab423e6d
msgid ""
"Before passing user input, the socket service will receive a null-terminated "
"service descriptor, i.e. the part after ``QUBESRPC``. When running in a VM, "
"this is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:24
#: 9782bc32f78943baa195ed9b6cd2d417
msgid "When running in dom0, it is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:32
#: 924c1104687e49d7beaf1b39581c5831
msgid ""
"(The target type can be ``name``, in which case target is a domain name, or "
"``keyword``, in which the target is a keyword like ``@dispvm``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:34
#: c018e39e0d154691baa1ae615b0ed48b
msgid ""
"Afterwards, data provided by the service’s user (as stdin) is sent into the "
"socket, and data received from the socket is sent back to the user (as "
"stdout). When the service closes the socket, an exit code of 0 is sent back "
"to the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:37
#: f2103529644d4da7821c729a11b805d7
msgid "Differences from executable-based services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:40
#: 80b1ee0746ca44edae7c33514e01ef73
msgid ""
"From the user point of view, the socket-based service behaves almost like an "
"executable-based one. Here are the differences:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:42
#: afedc30467404f3d9a5bc53c576a6276
msgid ""
"There is no stderr (the socket provides only one output stream). Currently, "
"that means stderr will also never be closed on user’s end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:44
#: 0dacd374bc884a35945c76ca7fb3089f
msgid ""
"There is no exit code. When the socket connection is closed, exit code 0 is "
"sent to the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:49
#: 4a40b5b6f51f4e0ebf2756e1dda88cf2
msgid "Recommended use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:52
#: fcc0d500e4db4b4bb9f887b69f909967
msgid ""
"Create a program that binds to path *outside* ``/etc/qubes-rpc``, such as ``/"
"var/run/my-daemon.sock``. Put a symlink in ``/etc/qubes-rpc``, e.g. ``ln -s /"
"var/run/my-daemon.sock /etc/qubes-rpc/qubes.Service``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:54
#: a5243a377f2b4678852853a4d4026690
msgid ""
"If your program handles multiple services, create multiple symlinks. You can "
"dispatch based on the service descriptor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/services/qrexec-socket-services.rst:56
#: 8ce230086f17402aa2376218549a833a
msgid "Do not run the program as root."
msgstr ""

